comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-04T16:55:18.325Z",claude-hub,"Fix (branch fix/release-version-targets-extension-export), against the issue's acceptance list. (1) scripts/release-identity.ts --write replaces the release workflow's first-match regex. It sets only the version property of 'export default defineExtension({ name: \"pm-jev\", version: ... })' and refuses a source with zero or several such declarations, or a version that is not plain x.y.z. The index.ts comment no longer quotes a version literal, and the export now declares the package version 2026.11.4 (it had said 2026.10.5 since v0). (2) release:check runs verify:release-identity right after the build. It compares package.json, both package-lock.json versions, manifest.json and the version property of the source and built default exports, which are imported statically and never activated, so a mismatch fails release preparation before commit or publish. (3) test/release-identity.test.ts runs the rewrite on a fixture with a misleading preceding comment, catalog_version, a nested version and a --policy-version example, then evaluates the module in a child process: the old first-match rewrite leaves the export stale, the new one updates only the export. (4) The pack step runs --archive on ./release-artifact/package.tgz. The packed package.json and manifest.json must report the verified version, and the packed dist/index.js must be byte-identical to the build whose export was verified. The packed module is not evaluated, since an extracted archive has no dependencies. (5) No approval, publish or credential step changed; coverage stays at 100/100/100 including the new script. Revert check: restoring 2026.10.5 fails 'this repository's source and built exports report its package version'. Full release:check passed locally up to changelog:check, which needed this item's entry."
